Let the embedder park the committing thread at a full FIFO in the background instead of a drop (Minato, patch 0030).

Why: patch 0027 commits a full FIFO's oldest command buffer in the background, which iOS refuses: its work is lost.
For an app that draws once in the background and uses the result after the return (a texture uploaded or rendered
while it keeps drawing frames) that loss shows as wrong pixels on the iPhone; Android's GPU runs in the background and
loses nothing. Now ANGLEMetalSetDeferralFull(park) gives the embedder that moment: park() returns 1 once it parked the
thread until the foreground (the loop then commits the FIFO in order), 0 at once when it does not park (the drop as
before). The FIFO's lock is not held while park() waits. ANGLEMetalDeferredParked counts the parks. The embedder
parks only once the app's onStop and its surfaces' surfaceDestroyed are answered, so no answer waits for a parked
thread (graphics/host's angle.m, behind MINATO_BACKGROUND_PARK).
For tests only, MINATO_ANGLE_DROP_DISCARDS=1 does to a dropped command buffer what iOS does to a background commit:
nothing of it reaches the GPU, ANGLE's bookkeeping completes it. The Mac's Metal would run it and hide the loss.
Test: graphics/tests/angle_deferral_full.mm (drop: dfull above 0 and the background's one upload lost; park: nothing
dropped, parked once, the upload kept).
Upstream: not planned (an embedder's deferral).
diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/mtl_command_buffer.mm b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/mtl_command_buffer.mm
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/mtl_command_buffer.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/mtl_command_buffer.mm
@@ -75,6 +75,21 @@
 std::atomic<uint64_t> gDeferredFull{0};
 // Minato (patch 0027): the waits for a deferred command buffer's result that went on without it.
